{"agent":"con-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_PATH_RESULT` lists `pathlib.Path.parent` and `_resolve` only retypes a node as `pathlib.Path` when it is a `Call`. `.parent` is an `Attribute`, so `_resolve(Path('a').parent)` is `pathlib.Path.parent`, not `pathlib.Path`. Given `Path('a').parent.replace('b')`, the counted name is `pathlib.Path.parent.replace`, which is not in `(\"os.replace\", \"pathlib.Path.replace\")`, so `os_replace` stays 0. The same input assigned first (`p = Path('a').parent`; `p.replace('b')`) is also missed: `visit_Assign` binds only when `_resolve(value) == \"pathlib.Path\"`. The new comment and tests claim path-result chaining is counted; they never exercise `.parent`, which is the entry in the new set this arm cannot see.","digest":"27e25fff5ff7ced3","family":"xai","location":"tests/architecture_guards_support.py:104","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/architecture_guards_support.py:104"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new parameter binder walks only `node.args.args`. A keyword-only or positional-only `Path` parameter is never bound. Given `def f(*, dest: Path):\\n    dest.replace(other)\\n` (or `def f(dest: Path, /): ...`), `_resolve` on the name returns nothing, so `dest.replace` is not an `os_replace` site.","digest":"779999f506e160c7","family":"xai","location":"tests/architecture_guards_support.py:198","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/architecture_guards_support.py:198"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":7376,"diff_sha":"8c69f693756d700b3cb4d90b0c7aa6511576cd9e6448a936e3e1a2e39b598ffe","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/DX-guard-path-replace","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":74.3,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,