{"agent":"con-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The three call sites now import and call `replace_path`, but this change never defines it: the manifest is only these five files and `fsio` is untouched. Importing `docindex`, `store._projection`, or `remote_ssh` therefore raises `ImportError` before any rename runs (for example `replace_path(target, self.path)` at docindex.py).","digest":"fafbfc6fa28b259d","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/infra/docindex.py:34","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/infra/docindex.py:34"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_resolve` types a call as `pathlib.Path` only when the callee is in `_PATH_RESULT`, which omits constructors that return a path such as `Path.home` and `Path.cwd`. Given `from pathlib import Path` and `Path.home().replace('b')` (or `Path.cwd().replace(dest)`), the callee resolves to `pathlib.Path.home`, the call is not retyped, and `os_replace` stays 0, so that atomic rename is still unguarded.","digest":"1459672a482c51e0","family":"xai","location":"tests/architecture_guards_support.py:174","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/architecture_guards_support.py:174"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":8119,"diff_sha":"dd067bbc5e411ee5066740dae8664a3a515d3ae8390723689b93286354c30e21","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/DX-guard-path-replace","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":89.6,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"5532c5def0fef762","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DX-guard-path-replace.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261111T222238Z-33294f00.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794435758.8309023,"family":"google","gate":"rubber_duck","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reason":"HTT