{"agent":"con-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The earlier ImportError still stands: this diff still only touches the five listed files and never defines `replace_path` (fsio is unchanged, and there is no `swap_file` either). `docindex.py`, `store/_projection.py`, and `remote_ssh.py` now import that name, so `import ddflow.infra.docindex` (and the other two modules) raises `ImportError` before `replace_path(target, self.path)` or the other call sites can run. Routing the renames through an undefined helper also drops them out of the `os_replace` counter, so the unguarded atomic renames the ratchet was meant to see are neither implemented nor counted.","digest":"72d48bb634373d13","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/infra/docindex.py:34","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/infra/docindex.py:34"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new parameter and `AnnAssign` binders only treat a bare `ast.Name` annotation as `pathlib.Path`. Given `import pathlib` and `def f(dest: pathlib.Path):\\n    dest.replace('b')` (or `x: pathlib.Path = pathlib.Path('a')` then `x.replace('b')`), the annotation is an `Attribute`, nothing is bound, `_resolve` does not yield `pathlib.Path.replace`, and `os_replace` stays 0. The same new `visit_Assign` only binds a plain `Name` target, so `self.path = Path('a')` followed by `self.path.replace('b')` is also uncounted.","digest":"1e896c8ae6e98931","family":"xai","location":"tests/architecture_guards_support.py:204","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/architecture_guards_support.py:204"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":8263,"diff_sha":"2ee6030b9cd583bff007737c4759cd2593128f4b83ab140024e0e26b57694c23","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/DX-guard-path-replace","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":71.